		{
			"id": "ePPyb3rkLMNLYLZOq",
			"description": "Meltagun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Imperium's dedicated close-range anti-armour infantry weapon, flash-vaporising the target's outer surface with a superheated fusion reaction; fiction across every era treats it as able to gut a tank at point-blank range and as nearly worthless at any distance, in sharp contrast to a lascannon's much longer reach.\n\nDesign: This is the project's fixed melta anchor: 8dx3(10) burn at ½D, \"much less beyond.\" Checked against the vehicle armour table: AV14 (DR 250, a Leman Russ or Land Raider's front) has effective DR 25 against the (10) armour divisor; 8dx3 averages 84, more than three times the effective DR, so it easily beats even the heaviest armour in the framework's table at ½D range, as the assignment requires. The sharp drop-off is modelled as a second weapon line rather than a formula: beyond ½D the round keeps only its base dice (4d burn), with neither the x3 multiplier nor the (10) armour divisor, representing the fusion reaction losing coherence in open air before it reaches the target. This is a deliberate departure from default GURPS range rules (which do not normally reduce damage with range) rather than an anchor conflict; it exists because the framework explicitly calls for \"much less beyond,\" and a flat halving of the anchor's own huge multiplier would still be an anti-tank weapon at any range, which the fiction does not support. ST 10 and a very short 10/50 range band (versus a boltgun's 200/1000) capture the weapon's role as a close-assault specialist, not a rifle.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
